            <ArticleTitle>Adverse events after administration of tetanus-diphtheria-acellular pertussis vaccine to healthcare workers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>389-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1086/596201</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Healthcare workers who received the tetanus-diphtheria-acellular pertussis (Tdap) vaccine were surveyed about adverse events. Local adverse events were more common among women and among those who received the Tdap vaccine less than 5 years after they had received the tetanus-diphtheria vaccine. Systemic adverse events were more common among healthcare workers aged less than 30 years. These findings provide guidance for counseling of healthcare workers who receive Tdap vaccine.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
